eq 1 \] sdtest hrs if wrkstat==1, by(sex) Variance ratio test ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ Group | Obs Mean Std. err. Std. dev. [95% conf. interval] ---------+-------------------------------------------------------------------- male | 748 48.08422 .4630884 12.66528 47.17512 48.99333 female | 671 43.6155 .4045276 10.47875 42.8212 44.40979 ---------+-------------------------------------------------------------------- Combined | 1,419 45.97111 .3156328 11.88977 45.35195 46.59026 ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ ratio = sd(male) / sd(female) f = 1.4609 H0: ratio = 1 Degrees of freedom = 747, 670 Ha: ratio &lt; 1 Ha: ratio != 1 Ha: ratio &gt; 1 Pr(F &lt; f) = 1.0000 2*Pr(F &gt; f) = 0.0000 Pr(F &gt; f) = 0.0000 We reject the null hypothesis and the variance between the two samples is not the same. This will matter when we focus on Analysis of Variance (ANOVA). In regression, one of assumption is constant variance across values or homoskedasticity.
